  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 240 PM CDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nThe surface low mentioned above along with a slow moving front looks \nto slide southeastward into Iowa over the weekend as an upper level \nshortwave pushes over the central and northern Rockies onto the \nPlains this weekend. These features will bring the next round of \nshowers and storms with the favorable heavy rainfall \nenvironment still over the region more so on Saturday than \nSunday. While there could end up being a few stronger storms, \nmore marginal lapse rates diminish this concern at this time. As\nthe upper level shortwave moves more over the state or \nimmediate vicinity, this will keep shower potential in place \ninto early next week. The intensity, coverage, and duration \nshould be less with time with - I hesitate to type - drier \nconditions towards Wednesday as the influence of surface high \npressure moves into the area. This may not be long-lived, but a \nbreak would be welcome for those Iowans that have seen enough \nrain.",
